Z||000000||fropuff||12-29-2001||05:45 PM||||Hey guys.  I plan on getting my 86 GT done early-spring, and I plan on drving it to school when I'm done.  However, my school has a few that like to vandalize/take sh*t that isn't theirs.  I plan on havng my Fiero well decked-out, with a CD player, amp, subs, etc.  This would be a heaven for the bastards.  I'm thinking about getting a security system for it.  I found one from Crutchfield that is connected to a pager.  I was also thinking about a video surveillance system.  I think this would be better, as it would be a sure-fire way to catch them and get my stuff back/get my damage paid for.  I found some 1.5" half-sphere 360-degree cameras, like the ones found in Wal-Mart/Target.  I would want to get four of them, to mount on each corner of the headliner, up-side down.  But, of course, this would all have to be connected to a recorder of some sort, like found in the banks; the ones that cycle through the cameras and record what's going on.  I would also need a power source of some sort.  Here's the question..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If I were to do something like this, how would I go about powering it?  I'm at school for about 6.5 hours, and it would surely kill the battery in that time.  That's question 1. Question 2 is: how much do you think this would cost?  The pager system is less than $150, so I could always go that route.  I hope you guys know what I'm talking about.  Thanks a lot for any help.  Have a good one!<P>PS: If any of you guys are in the surveillance business that could hook me up, that'd be great!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks again!||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-29-2001||06:19 PM||||well, you could park it with a Rotweiler inside that has been on a steady diet of shotgun shells and acid - that might scare them away a little bit<P> Do you have the option of parking it where you can keep an eye on it?<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||12-29-2001||06:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>...Do you have the option of parking it where you can keep an eye on it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>-Where the location of the lot is, I cannot see it from any of my classes throughout the day.  Other classes can see the lot, but it doesn't stop the kids from doing sh*t.  I walked up on a girl looking in my windows for rear speakers/CD player, also saw them carrying lock-opening tools (slim-jim, etc), and my driver's door lock was tampered with.  Now I can't open it from that side with the key.  I don't know why they would do this, I have stock speakers, no subs, and the Delco tape deck.  I don't leave my cell phone in there anymore though.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||12-29-2001||10:11 PM||||I have seen people replace their door locks with pick proof locks(round key). You could make some steel plates to cover your side glass, all you need to do is to figure out how to lock them on. I've seen these on construction equipment to prevent vandalism. They could be made to fit between the dew wipe and glass and hooked to the top of the rolled up glass. J.C. Whitney use to carry the locks, I don't know if they do anymore. These type of modifications would practically make your car impregnable. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||12-29-2001||10:27 PM||||What about the sunroof?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  That's the easiest frickin thing to get into.  I've been known to use it in a pinch with the keys locked in.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Actually, I'm not really worried about theft that much; I'm worried about my new mint condition paint getting keyed. It happened last year on the hood; nice 3' long scratch.  I knew who it was, but there was no witesses or evidence to show that the bastard did it.  If I'm not mistaken, I don't think I had to sign a waiver that said the school was not responsible for theft/damage.  I could always try that.  The thing that bugs me is that the whole school knows the kids stay out there all day smoking and whatnot, but nothing is ever done.  I brought up a hell of a fuss when my lock was f-d up.  But they didn't give a crap.  I just want a system that will assure me that if my car is f**ked with, I can find out who did it and get my stuff back, or have them pay for the damage done to my car.  I think it would only take one time for all to learn not to mess with me.  Any ideas?  Thanks again!  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TylerB11||12-30-2001||12:13 AM||||Its doable, with minimum power requirements. Check out X-10 (www.x10.com) they make some very small, and very cheap cameras, and recording systems. If you need help designing a system, PM me.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-30-2001||12:22 AM||||Id rent someplace to keep the car, buy a beater car for school for a few hundred dollars. I know a girlfriend who keeps her nice car in an elderly ladies garage for a few bucks a month just off campus. I rent a storage garage at a U-lock it place, share it with Lisa, so it makes it cheap for both of us.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-30-2001).]||||reg||1
